## 9. Headless Domain Controller Service

A systemd user service was implemented to manage the Windows Server VM independently of an interactive desktop session.

### Configuration

```ini
[Unit]
Description=Active Directory Domain Controller VM

[Service]
Type=exec
ExecStart=/usr/lib/virtualbox/VBoxHeadless --startvm <REDACTED-VM-UUID>
ExecStop=%h/.local/bin/<shutdown-helper>.sh
TimeoutStopSec=300
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=15

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
```

The service was configured for automatic startup, and user lingering was enabled.

### Verification

```text
Service enabled: yes
Service active: yes
User lingering: yes
VM process: VBoxHeadless
Domain authentication: successful
```

### Operational Caveat

The shutdown helper requests an ACPI shutdown and waits for the VM to power off.

Previous ACPI shutdown testing did not consistently result in a completed Windows shutdown.

The current configuration also uses systemd's default control-group process termination behavior.

Therefore, graceful shutdown during a full Linux host shutdown has **not yet been validated**.

This remains an operational risk and must be addressed before the environment is treated as production-ready.

