## 11. Risk Assessment

| Risk | Impact | Priority | Planned action |
|---|---|---|---|
| Domain controller depends on everyday workstation | Authentication outage when host unavailable | High | Evaluate dedicated always-on host |
| Clean host shutdown unverified | VM or directory data integrity risk | High | Validate shutdown and recovery procedures |
| Supported AD backup not yet validated | Potential directory recovery failure | High | Implement and test system-state backups |
| Single domain controller | Single point of failure | High | Document availability and recovery strategy |
| DNS depends on domain controller | Domain service interruption | Medium–High | Document DNS dependencies and outage behavior |
| Administrative access model incomplete | Inconsistent privilege assignments | Medium | Implement least-privilege access matrix |
| Endpoint inventory incomplete | Limited visibility into household devices | Medium | Complete asset discovery |
| Centralized monitoring incomplete | Delayed fault detection | Medium | Deploy availability and log monitoring |

These ratings are preliminary and will be refined during the formal risk assessment.

